Build Performance Test

Detailed description on how performance test are run can be found on Perfor=
mance Test<https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Performance_Test> wiki. The b=
elow charts are displaying the build performance trend for 1.8 by milestone=
 starting 1.6 on Master. The charts by Milestone can be accessed at this li=
nk<https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/charts/perf_milestone/performance_test.htm=
l> where you can view more detailed information or by clicking on the image=
s which will open a new window with the interactive chart.
=1B$B!x=1B(B  Building the Kernel remained fairly the same on both Ubuntu a=
nd Fedora hosts, since no major updates were performed between rc1 and rc2
=1B$B!x=1B(B  The rootfs build time improved with few seconds, now having 4=
:19 on Ubuntu and 4:22 on Fedora.
=1B$B!x=1B(B  Due to the latest libtool upstream changes, we have a spike i=
n performance when building the core-image-sato with rm-work. The RC2 take =
with an average of 11 minutes longer. We have 1:19:37 against 1:08:11 hours=
 on Ubuntu and 1:22:15 against 1:11:18 hours on Fedora. Some fixes have bee=
n made, with notable improvements in the latest master (1:13:52 on Ubuntu a=
nd 1:16:13 on Fedora).

Overall we can see small improvements in building the Kernel and rootfs but=
 a notable degradation when building the image with rm-work.



